    {'heading': 'Prāṇāyāma · restraining the breath'},
    {'rubric': "While the breath is drawn in, held and let out, the seven vyāhṛtis (each with oṃ), the Gāyatrī and its 'head' are recited mentally. The book prints the vyāhṛtis abbreviated ('oṃ bhūḥ &c.'); they are written out here."},
    {'padas': ['oṃ bhūḥ | oṃ bhuvaḥ | oṃ suvaḥ | oṃ mahaḥ | oṃ janaḥ | oṃ tapaḥ | oṃ satyam |', 'oṃ tatsa^vi_turvare^ṇyaṃ_ bhargo^ de_vasya^ dhīmahi | dhiyo_ yo naḥ^ praco_dayā^t ||', "omāpo jyotī raso'mṛtaṃ brahma bhūrbhuvaḥ suvarom ||"], 'num': '', 'gloss': "Oṃ the earth, the mid-region, heaven, and the higher worlds — mahas, janas, tapas, satya. We meditate on that choice splendour of the god Savitṛ; may he impel our thoughts. Oṃ — the waters, the light, the savour, the deathless, Brahman, earth, sky, heaven: oṃ. (Gāyatrī: ṚV 3.62.10 / TS 1.5.6; the 'head': Taittirīya Āraṇyaka 10.)"},
