    {'heading': 'Mārjana · sprinkling'},
    {'rubric': 'Water is sprinkled on the head, at each foot of the verse. ṚV 10.9.1–3, also TS 4.1.5.'},
    {'padas': ['āpo_ hi ṣṭhā ma^yo_bhuva_stā na^ ū_rje da^dhātana |', 'ma_he raṇā^ya_ cakṣa^se ||'], 'num': '|| 1 ||', 'gloss': 'Waters, you are the bringers of well-being: so set us in strength, for great and joyous sight.'},
    {'padas': ['yo vaḥ^ śi_vata^mo_ rasa_stasya^ bhājayate_ha naḥ^ |', 'u_śa_tīri^va mā_taraḥ^ ||'], 'num': '|| 2 ||', 'gloss': 'Give us here a share of your most blessed essence, like loving mothers.'},
    {'padas': ['tasmā_ araṃ^ gamāma vo_ yasya_ kṣayā^ya_ jinva^tha |', 'āpo^ ja_naya^thā ca naḥ ||'], 'num': '|| 3 ||', 'gloss': 'May we come fully to that, waters, for whose dwelling you quicken us; and make us fruitful.'},
    {'heading': 'Prāśana · sipping the water'},
    {'rubric': 'A little water is taken in the palm and sipped with the mantra for the time of day (Taittirīya Āraṇyaka 10.23–25). These Āraṇyaka mantras are shown without svaras: no accented public-domain text of them could be read.'},
    {'padas': ['sūryaśca mā manyuśca manyupatayaśca manyukṛtebhyaḥ | pāpebhyo rakṣantām | yadrātryā pāpamakārṣam |', 'manasā vācā hastābhyām | padbhyāmudareṇa śiśnā | rātristadavalumpatu |', 'yatkiñca duritaṃ mayi | idamahaṃ māmamṛtayonau | sūrye jyotiṣi juhomi svāhā ||'], 'num': '', 'gloss': 'Morning. May Sūrya, Manyu and the lords of Manyu guard me from the sins that anger has done. Whatever sin I did in the night — with mind, speech, hands, feet, belly or sex — may the night wipe it away. Whatever evil is in me, this, and myself, I offer into the deathless source, into Sūrya, the light: svāhā.', 'prose': True},
    {'rubric': "Evening: agniśca for sūryaśca, ahnā for rātryā, ahas for rātriḥ, and satye for sūrye — 'what I did in the day, may the day wipe away … I offer into the true light'."},
    {'padas': ['āpaḥ punantu pṛthivīṃ pṛthivī pūtā punātu mām | punantu brahmaṇaspatiḥ brahmapūtā punātu mām |', "yaducchiṣṭamabhojyaṃ yadvā duścaritaṃ mama | sarvaṃ punantu māmāpo'satāṃ ca pratigrahaṃ svāhā ||"], 'num': '', 'gloss': 'Noon. May the waters purify the earth; may the earth, purified, purify me. May they purify the Lord of the Veda; may the Veda, pure, purify me. Whatever I have eaten as leavings or unfit food, whatever wrong I have done, gifts taken from the unworthy — may the waters purify me of all: svāhā.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': 'Punar-mārjana · the second sprinkling'},
    {'rubric': 'ṚV 4.39.6, also TS 1.5.11; then āpo hi ṣṭhā again.'},
    {'padas': ['da_dhi_krāvṇo^ akāriṣaṃ ji_ṣṇoraśva^sya vā_jinaḥ^ |', 'su_ra_bhi no_ mukhā^ kara_tpra ṇa_ āyūṃ^ṣi tāriṣat ||'], 'num': '', 'gloss': 'I have praised Dadhikrāvan, the victorious, swift steed: may he make our mouths fragrant and lengthen our lives.'},
    {'heading': 'Arghya · the offering of water'},
    {'rubric': "Standing, water is thrown up towards the sun with the Gāyatrī: three times at dawn and dusk (and two at noon, in the book's account). ṚV 3.62.10, also TS 1.5.6."},
    {'padas': ['oṃ tatsa^vi_turvare^ṇyaṃ_ bhargo^ de_vasya^ dhīmahi |', 'dhiyo_ yo naḥ^ praco_dayā^t ||'], 'num': '', 'gloss': 'Oṃ. We meditate on that choice splendour of the god Savitṛ; may he impel our thoughts.'},
    {'rubric': 'Water is thrown round oneself in a ring; then, looking at the sun and touching the heart:'},
