    {'heading': 'Gāyatrī āvāhana · inviting the Gāyatrī'},
    {'rubric': 'After prāṇāyāma, water is sprinkled on the head. Taittirīya Āraṇyaka 10.26 (unaccented, as above).'},
    {'padas': ['āyātu varadā devī akṣaraṃ brahmasammitam |', 'gāyatrī chandasāṃ mātā idaṃ brahma juṣasva naḥ ||'], 'num': '|| 1 ||', 'gloss': 'May the boon-giving goddess come, the imperishable, measured with Brahman: Gāyatrī, mother of the metres — make this Brahman welcome to us. (The book notes the variant juṣasva me.)'},
    {'padas': ["ojo'si saho'si balamasi bhrājo'si devānāṃ dhāma nāmāsi viśvamasi viśvāyuḥ sarvamasi sarvāyuḥ abhibhūrom |", 'gāyatrīmāvāhayāmi ||'], 'num': '|| 2 ||', 'gloss': "You are vigour, you are might, strength and radiance; you are the gods' abode and name; you are all, all life; the whole, whole life; the overcomer — oṃ. I invite the Gāyatrī.", 'prose': True},
    {'heading': 'Nyāsa · placing'},
    {'rubric': 'The book notes these placings as later (Tāntric) additions now generally done. Karanyāsa — the fingers, named in pairs:'},
    {'padas': ['aṅguṣṭhābhyāṃ namaḥ | tarjanībhyāṃ namaḥ | madhyamābhyāṃ namaḥ |', 'anāmikābhyāṃ namaḥ | kaniṣṭhikābhyāṃ namaḥ | karatalakarapṛṣṭhābhyāṃ namaḥ ||'], 'num': '', 'gloss': 'Homage to the thumbs, the forefingers, the middle fingers, the ring fingers, the little fingers, the palms and backs of the hands.', 'prose': True},
    {'rubric': 'Aṅganyāsa — the six parts of the Gāyatrī placed on the heart, head, crest, chest (as a shield), eyes, and round the head (as a weapon):'},
    {'padas': ['tatsavituḥ brahmātmane hṛdayāya namaḥ | vareṇyaṃ viṣṇvātmane śirase svāhā |', 'bhargo devasya rudrātmane śikhāyai vaṣaṭ | dhīmahi satyātmane kavacāya hum |', 'dhiyo yo naḥ jñānātmane netradvayāya vauṣaṭ | pracodayāt paramātmane astrāya phaṭ ||'], 'num': '', 'gloss': "'That of Savitṛ' — to Brahmā, homage to the heart. 'Choice' — to Viṣṇu, to the head. 'Splendour of the god' — to Rudra, to the crest. 'We meditate' — to Truth, to the shield. 'Who our thoughts' — to Knowledge, to the two eyes (variant: the three eyes). 'May impel' — to the Supreme Self, to the weapon.", 'prose': True},
    {'heading': 'Japa'},
    {'rubric': 'The Gāyatrī (as at the arghya) is then repeated mentally, generally 108 times.'},
    {'heading': 'Upasthāna · standing before the sun'},
    {'rubric': 'Bidding the Gāyatrī farewell (Āraṇyaka, unaccented):'},
    {'padas': ['uttame śikhare devī bhūmyāṃ parvatamūrdhani |', "brāhmaṇebhyo'bhyanujñātā gaccha devi yathāsukham ||"], 'num': '', 'gloss': "On the high peak at the mountain's summit, rooted in the earth, the goddess dwells: given leave by the brāhmaṇas, go, goddess, as you please. (Book variants: jāte; abhyanujñānam.)"},
    {'rubric': 'Contemplation before the upasthāna, Taittirīya Āraṇyaka 10.31 (unaccented):'},
    {'padas': ['omantaścarati bhūteṣu guhāyāṃ viśvamūrtiṣu |', 'tvaṃ yajñastvaṃ viṣṇustvaṃ vaṣaṭkārastvaṃ rudrastvaṃ brahmā tvaṃ prajāpatiḥ ||'], 'num': '', 'gloss': 'Oṃ — he moves within beings, in the cave of the heart, in all forms. You are the sacrifice, Viṣṇu, the vaṣaṭ-call, Rudra, Brahmā, Prajāpati.'},
    {'heading': 'Morning upasthāna · to Mitra'},
    {'rubric': 'TS 3.4.11 (cf. ṚV 3.59.6, 1–2).'},
    {'padas': ['mi_trasya^ carṣaṇī_dhṛta_ḥ śravo^ de_vasya^ sāna_sim |', 'sa_tyaṃ ci_traśra^vastamam ||'], 'num': '|| 1 ||', 'gloss': 'The glory of the god Mitra, upholder of peoples, worth winning, true, most wondrous in renown — (we sing).'},
    {'padas': ['mi_tro janā^nyātayati prajā_nanmi_tro dā^dhāra pṛthi_vīmu_ta dyām |', 'mi_traḥ kṛ_ṣṭīrani^miṣā_bhi ca^ṣṭe sa_tyāya^ ha_vyaṃ ghṛ_tava^dvidhema ||'], 'num': '|| 2 ||', 'gloss': 'Mitra, knowing, sets men to their work; Mitra upholds earth and heaven; Mitra watches the peoples unwinking. To the True one we offer an oblation rich with ghee.'},
    {'padas': ['pra sa mi^tra_ marto^ astu_ praya^svā_nyaste^ āditya_ śikṣa^ti vra_tena^ |', 'na ha^nyate_ na jī^yate_ tvoto_ naina_magṃho^ aśno_tyanti^to_ na dū_rāt ||'], 'num': '|| 3 ||', 'gloss': 'Mitra, Āditya — may the mortal who serves you by his rite be rich in food. Guarded by you he is not slain, not overcome; no sin reaches him, near or far.'},
    {'heading': 'Noon upasthāna'},
    {'padas': ['ā sa_tyena_ raja^sā_ varta^māno nive_śaya^nna_mṛtaṃ_ martyaṃ^ ca |', 'hi_ra_ṇyaye^na savi_tā rathe_nā de_vo yā^ti_ bhuva^nā vi_paśya^n ||'], 'num': '|| 1 ||', 'gloss': 'Turning through the true realm, settling the immortal and the mortal in their places, the god Savitṛ comes in his golden chariot, beholding the worlds. (TS 3.4.11; ṚV 1.35.2 reads ā kṛṣṇena … bhuvanāni paśyan.)'},
    {'padas': ['udvayaṃ tamasaspari paśyanto jyotiruttaram |', 'devaṃ devatrā sūryamaganma jyotiruttamam ||'], 'num': '|| 2 ||', 'gloss': 'Beholding the higher light beyond the darkness, we have come to Sūrya, god among the gods, the highest light. (TS 4.1.7 reading; unaccented — no legible accented TS text of it was found.)'},
    {'padas': ['udu_ tyaṃ jā_tave^dasaṃ de_vaṃ va^hanti ke_tavaḥ^ |', 'dṛ_śe viśvā^ya_ sūrya^m ||'], 'num': '|| 3 ||', 'gloss': 'His rays bear up the god who knows all beings, Sūrya, for all to see. (ṚV 1.50.1, TS 1.4.43.)'},
    {'padas': ['ci_traṃ de_vānā_muda^gā_danī^kaṃ_ cakṣu^rmi_trasya_ varu^ṇasyā_gneḥ |', 'āprā_ dyāvā^pṛthi_vī a_ntari^kṣaṃ_ sūrya^ ā_tmā jaga^tasta_sthuṣa^śca ||'], 'num': '|| 4 ||', 'gloss': 'The bright face of the gods has risen, the eye of Mitra, Varuṇa and Agni; it has filled heaven, earth and the mid-air. Sūrya is the self of all that moves and stands. (ṚV 1.115.1, TS 1.4.43.)'},
    {'padas': ['taccakṣurdevahitaṃ purastācchukramuccarat | paśyema śaradaḥ śatam | jīvema śaradaḥ śatam |', 'nandāma śaradaḥ śatam | modāma śaradaḥ śatam | bhavāma śaradaḥ śatam | śṛṇavāma śaradaḥ śatam |', 'prabravāma śaradaḥ śatam | ajītāḥ syāma śaradaḥ śatam | jyokca sūryaṃ dṛśe |', "ya udagānmahato'rṇavādvibhrājamānaḥ sarirasya madhyāt |", 'sa mā vṛṣabho lohitākṣaḥ sūryo vipaścinmanasā punātu ||'], 'num': '|| 5 ||', 'gloss': 'That eye, set by the gods, rises bright in the east: may we see a hundred autumns, live a hundred, rejoice, delight, prosper, hear and speak a hundred autumns; unconquered may we be a hundred autumns, and long see the sun. He who has risen shining from the great ocean, from the midst of the waters — may that bull, red-eyed Sūrya, the wise, purify me in mind. (Taittirīya Āraṇyaka 4; unaccented.)', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': 'Evening upasthāna · to Varuṇa'},
    {'padas': ['i_maṃ me^ varuṇa śrudhī_ hava^ma_dyā ca^ mṛḍaya |', 'tvāma^va_syurā ca^ke ||'], 'num': '|| 1 ||', 'gloss': 'Hear this call of mine, Varuṇa, and be gracious today; longing for your help I cry to you. (ṚV 1.25.19, TS 2.1.11.)'},
    {'padas': ['tattvā^ yāmi_ brahma^ṇā_ vanda^māna_stadā śā^ste_ yaja^māno ha_virbhiḥ^ |', 'ahe^ḍamāno varuṇe_ha bo_dhyuru^śagṃsa_ mā na_ āyuḥ_ pra mo^ṣīḥ ||'], 'num': '|| 2 ||', 'gloss': 'Praising you with this prayer I come to you for that which the sacrificer seeks with his offerings. Be here without anger, Varuṇa, and heed us, widely praised; do not take away our life. (ṚV 1.24.11, TS 2.1.11.)'},
    {'padas': ['yacci_ddhi te_ viśo^ yathā_ pra de^va varuṇa vra_tam |', 'mi_nī_masi_ dyavi^dyavi ||'], 'num': '|| 3 ||', 'gloss': 'Whatever law of yours, god Varuṇa, we break day after day, as people do — (forgive it). (ṚV 1.25.1, TS 3.4.11.)'},
    {'padas': ["yatkiṃ ce_daṃ va^ruṇa_ daivye_ jane^'bhidro_haṃ ma^nu_ṣyā^ścarā^masi |", 'aci^ttī_ yattava_ dharmā^ yuyopi_ma mā na_stasmā_dena^so deva rīriṣaḥ ||'], 'num': '|| 4 ||', 'gloss': 'Whatever wrong we humans do against the divine folk, Varuṇa, whatever law of yours we have blurred unknowing — do not harm us for that sin, god. (ṚV 7.89.5, TS 3.4.11.)'},
    {'padas': ['ki_ta_vāso_ yadri^ri_purna dī_vi yadvā^ ghā sa_tyamu_ta yanna vi_dma |', 'sarvā_ tā viṣya^ śithi_reva^ de_vāthā^ te syāma varuṇa pri_yāsaḥ^ ||'], 'num': '|| 5 ||', 'gloss': 'Whatever cheats have charged against us, as at dice, whatever we did knowingly or did not know — loosen it all, god, as if slack; then may we be dear to you, Varuṇa. (TS 3.4.11; ṚV 5.85.8 reads devādhā.)'},
